# ── Benchmark recording outputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per CLAUDE.md → Recording → Durability: git is authoritative for SMALL TEXT
# (results.json, metadata.json, 0_README.md, notes.md, cmd.txt, pre/, post/, and the
# summary CSVs at the runs/ root — all COMMITTED). S3 is authoritative for the heavy
# write-once telemetry below, which must NOT enter git.
runs/*/raw/
runs/*/cmd.log
runs/sweep-logs/

# runs/.leg-state/ is deliberately NOT ignored — it is TRACKED, and must stay tracked.
#
# It holds run-leg.sh's per-step completion markers. The instance is rebuilt at least
# twice, and these markers are the only thing that stops a resumed leg from re-running
# steps it already completed: without them a rebuilt `run-leg.sh --leg $LEG` silently
# redoes hours of sweeps into duplicate timestamped run dirs, polluting the aggregates
# rather than erroring.
#
# git carries them rather than S3 for two reasons: CLAUDE.md's authority split makes
# git authoritative for all small text, and S3's never-delete archive semantics would
# resurrect a marker deleted on purpose to force a re-run. Teardown commits everything
# anyway, which is exactly the moment these need to be captured.

# Large per-workload telemetry CSVs — per-interval output balloons on long endurance
# cells (hundreds of MB each), exceeds GitHub per-file limits, and is regenerable from
# the raw output that is already excluded. Headline numbers live in the summary CSVs.
**/workload-*.csv

# Defensive: catch the same patterns at any depth, in case a subtree is ever added.
**/runs/*/raw/
**/runs/*/cmd.log
**/runs/sweep-logs/

# ── Secrets / credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.env
*.pem
*.key
credentials*
.aws/

# The filled-in configuration, at the repo root. env.example.sh IS tracked (it's the
# template and the documented list of every variable); env.sh holds real values and
# stays local — which is why the environment contract in S3 is how it is recovered
# after a rebuild.
env.sh

# ── Local scratch (mounted outside the repo; defensive) ────────────────────────
/data/

